                  }
                 }
                ],
                "text": "MOA"
               },
               {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": cortisol, as well as other steroid hormones, binds to intracellular receptors – the steroid-receptor complex enters the nucleus and acts as a transcription factor to turn on certain genes, causing synthesis of specific proteins which are responsible for its physiological actions"
               }
              ]
             },
             {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "attrs": {
               "indLeft": 0,
               "indRight": 0,
               "indFirst": 0,
               "spaceBefore": 0,
